## False Positives

Potential legitimate causes include:

- User password mistakes
- Password changes
- Expired passwords
- Cached credentials
- Mapped drives using stale credentials
- Services using outdated passwords
- Scheduled tasks using stale credentials
- Application authentication failures
- Administrative troubleshooting
- Authorized security testing

---

## Tuning Recommendations

Production tuning could include:

- Establishing normal authentication-failure baselines
- Increasing or decreasing the failure threshold
- Adjusting the detection window
- Identifying service accounts
- Identifying known noisy applications
- Correlating source IP addresses
- Considering account privilege/sensitivity
- Detecting one source targeting many accounts
- Detecting many sources targeting one account
- Correlating subsequent successful authentication
- Correlating endpoint activity following authentication

Potential future detections could separate:

```text
Many Passwords → One Account
```

from:

```text
One/Few Passwords → Many Accounts
```

rather than treating all authentication failures as the same behavior.

